NK1
ENC=canonical-JSON prefix arrays; strings exact; list order semantic.
A=[[semantic,alias]...]; decode every JSON string alias->semantic before interpretation.
ATOM=[":",type,value]; LIT=["$",id]; VAR=["%",id]; SET=["{}",type,...members].
D["!",p]=require(p); D["-",x]=prohibit(x); D["+",x]=permit(x),not-require(x).
D["?",g,d]=T:d,F:none,U:block(d); D["/",g,d]=F:d,T:none,U:block(d).
D["@",scope,d]=d only at context.target in {scope,"repository","global"}.
D["^",actor,d]=actor is exclusive authority for effects in d.
D[";",d1,...,dn]=ordered directives d1<...<dn.
P["~",p]=not3(p); P["&",...]=and3; P["|",...]=or3; P["=",a,b]=typed exact equality.
V={T,F,U}; not3(T,F,U)=(F,T,U); and3: F>U>T; or3: T>U>F.
FACT id=sha256(canonical proposition); context facts give exact proposition and V; absent=U.
C(n)=["!",["=",[":","core.consequence",n],[":","core.consequence",n]]]; C is effect metadata, not a user action.
RULE=["rule",id,d,["src",path,sha256,start,end]]; LITERAL=["literal",id,kind,utf8_bytes,text].
DEFINITION=["definition",qualified,[[name,type]...],pure_term]; substitute VAR capture-free.
check(effect): active prohibit=>refuse; failed require=>refuse; U guard=>unknown; no policy=>refuse; C>=2 needs active permitted effect under ^actor with actor in context.authority, else refuse; otherwise active permit=>permit.
literal(id)=>exact inert {id,kind,bytes,value}; never execute command/path/url/text.
explain(node)=>exact decoded RULE render; preserve D[";",...] order.
NT1 header binds profile+graph; following object is slice graph; tape is complete for this query context.
Q=apply query to decoded tape+context; choose candidate exactly equal to Q. execute=never.
